      "side": 1,
      "message": "Not a full review yet, but there\u0027s something that doesn\u0027t quite work right when the same block is emitted multiple times (due to the way that certain blocks are inlined).\n\nFor example, this function doesn\u0027t produce valid IR:\n```\n       %main \u003d OpFunction %void None %ep_type\n %main_start \u003d OpLabel\n          %1 \u003d OpCopyObject %i32 %one\n               OpBranchConditional %true %bb_true %bb_true\n    %bb_true \u003d OpLabel\n          %2 \u003d OpCopyObject %i32 %two\n         %22 \u003d OpCopyObject %i32 %2\n               OpReturn\n               OpFunctionEnd\n```\n\nIR:\n```\nFailed to parse SPIR-V: :12:22 error: let: %3 is not in scope\n        %6:i32 \u003d let %3\n                     ^^\n\n:10:7 note: in block\n      $B3: {  # false\n      ^^^\n\n:6:9 note: %3 declared here\n        %3:i32 \u003d let 2i\n        ^^^^^^\n\nnote: # Disassembly\n%main \u003d @compute @workgroup_size(1u, 1u, 1u) func():void {\n  $B1: {\n    %2:i32 \u003d let 1i\n    if true [t: $B2, f: $B3] {  # if_1\n      $B2: {  # true\n        %3:i32 \u003d let 2i\n        %4:i32 \u003d let %3\n        ret\n      }\n      $B3: {  # false\n        %5:i32 \u003d let 2i\n        %6:i32 \u003d let %3\n        ret\n      }\n    }\n    unreachable\n  }\n}\n```",
      "revId": "79c039d251871e99f359451291fed28c5792c9c2",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
